Project Scope Structure

[Project Name]
Business Approval: Approach and Plan

1. Executive Summary
A concise explanation of the business problem, urgency, scope,
recommended solution and expected outcome.

2. Proposed Approach
The recommended delivery approach, how it will operate, why it has
been selected and the controls or benefits it provides.

3. Solution Architecture
A visual representation of the end-to-end solution, covering source,
processing, integration, target and assurance controls.

4. Delivery Phases and Contingency
The gated delivery path from discovery through proof of concept,
pilot, full implementation and closure, including fallback arrangements.

5. Project Execution
The practical delivery journey, showing responsibilities, inputs,
outputs, stakeholder engagement and sign-off points.

6. Plan on a Page
An integrated timeline showing workstreams, key activities,
dependencies, milestones, decisions and project status.

7. Key Risks
The principal risks, their potential impacts, mitigations and owners.

8. Key Assumptions
The conditions on which the plan depends, together with ownership
and actions required to validate each assumption.

